// form-knowledge-qwen-heldout-v3-eval.fk -- pinned, two-row-per-family audit (authored blind; see BLINDNESS below).
//
// V3 is an independent denominator authored after the fifteen-row lexical set
// became development-visible.  Thirty current-source facts are held only in
// this cell: two for each of the same fifteen repository families.  Each row
// binds the present source bytes, prompt, answer, answer hash, typed verifier,
// split, and authorship snapshot into one dataset seal.
//
// BLINDNESS, AS IT STANDS. The set was authored blind on 2026-08-24 (fkh3-authored). On
// 2026-10-03 the rows whose sources had drifted were re-pinned AFTER their facts were read
// against the sources: v301 v302 v305-v316 v319-v321 v323-v328 v330 took a new source sha and keep
// their question and answer; v322 and v329 pinned sources that no longer stood (a deleted
// recipe, a count a document no longer states) and were replaced by rows read from sources that
// stand. Those 26 rows are no longer blind; the blindness claim holds only for v303, v304, v317
// and v318. On 2026-10-11 v301 v302 v312 v314 v316 v321 v329 were re-pinned the same way: each
// source had moved, and each fact was read in it first (CAN-not-MUST; "one interface among many";
// "the first candidate offered"; the line <unix-seconds> <cmd-bytes> <out-bytes>; mac, windows,
// android; host-exec's optag 136; sixteen questions asked twice). There is no sealing door: the
// pins and the dataset seal below are literals typed in this file, and the band recomputes the
// source shas and the dataset sha and checks them.
//
// This cell never runs a model.  Its public renderers carry only row ids,
// families, scalar evidence, counts, and dataset/audit hashes.  Prompts,
// expected text, source excerpts, source paths, answer hashes, and generated
// text remain inside the evaluator.  A live door that asks a model is
// dataset-bound and consent-bound; form-cli-peer-heldout-direct-learning.fk
// scores a returned direct answer against a row here.
//
// Every row currently uses exact-normalized-v1: the whole normalized answer
// must be one of the variants authored and sealed here.  F1 and sequence stay
// visible diagnostics, but promotion is the minimum of their conservative
// score and the typed semantic score.  Thus lexical overlap cannot pass a row.
// No remote judge participates.
//
import form-stdlib/form-knowledge-qwen-heldout-eval.fk;
